Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0033 (touches nvidia/dspark.py,
spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py, spec_decode/depth_policy.py, worker/gpu/model_runner.py). Logging only:
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_LOG_FEATURES=1 with VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_LOG (patch 0023) adds two features of each draft to the round log,
"f": [margin_1, p1_1, ..., margin_k, p1_k]: the (top-1 - top-2) logit margin and the top-1 probability of the draft
logits (base + Markov bias) over the whole vocabulary, from each rank's shard and one more all-gather of [rows, 3]
(top-1, top-2, logsumexp) a Markov step. The local draft argmax takes its unfused path under the flag (the draft is the
same token). Why: the depth policy (0010) reads only the confidence head, whose first-position AUC on our panel is 0.83
on writing and 0.82 on chat against 0.90 on code; a replay of the depth rule with a sharper predictor (AUC ~0.94)
gives +6% tok/s on those domains (Oct 21). A log under fixed:k says whether these features carry that information.
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_LOG_HIDDEN=1 also writes the confidence head's inputs per draft position (the drafter's hidden at the
sampled position + the Markov embedding of the previous token, 5,376 bf16 values) to <log>.hid, one k x width record a
logged line ("h": its index), ~54 KB a round: training data for a better acceptance predictor on our own target.
Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_conf_features.py (serve image).

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/dspark.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/dspark.py
